NEW DEFECTS INTRODUCED BY THE ROUND-29 REVISION:
  - The P1a-R/P3-R split makes previously impossible phase gates satisfiable by moving the unresolved boundaries off every release path. That resolves the *gate contradiction* but not the brief’s whole-tree and human-approval requirements.

NEWLY RAISED FINDINGS (not previously an issue in any round):
  - `P3(7b')` simultaneously asserts that its displayed approval UI is unreachable and says its reachability from synthetic input is unmeasured. These are incompatible descriptions of the **same process-route UI**, not merely different UI routes.

